   "body": "/claim cloud/lot-131-opus\n\nPlan (M4 wave, #893):\n- Spec `docs/lots/LOT-131-blacklist-mpstorage.md` from the template: legacy `MPStorage.m` blacklist part + `BlackList.m:37-69` @ `87fe0d1c`, consent per account (LOT-130 `writeConsent`), pending captures listed, none hand-built.\n- App: a blocklist ↔ MPStorage bridge for the current account. Local add/remove stays local-first (LOT-061 store), then a LOT-062 edit through `MPStorageSyncModel.edit` only while the record is `on`; after a successful sync, the document's blocklist is **merged** into the local one (union-style, never `replaceBlocklist` with an empty remote list; removals carried only by the edit we wrote).\n- Consent: the first blocklist write with the record `unasked` asks (« Synchroniser la liste noire via le stockage MP ? »), then `setEnabled(true)`; `declined`/`off`/unreadable → device only.\n- State-changing: no new forum write path; only LOT-130's `sync` (session check, success on HFR's confirmation, `unconfirmed` kept pending, never re-sent blindly). Nothing in the « MP multiples → dark topic » switch (#1014).\n- Tests (Swift Testing, `App/SwiftHFRTests/MPStorage/`): empty remote never empties local, merge both ways, consent per state, no edit when not `on`; each shown failing without the change. Draft PR + `compile-check`, Fable adversarial review.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
